  <h2>When to Use Each Metric: Decision Framework</h2>
  <div class="table-responsive">
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Best Metric</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Comparing two markets</td><td><strong>Cap Rate</strong></td><td>Financing-neutral; apples-to-apples comparison</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Evaluating a specific deal with your loan</td><td><strong>Cash-on-Cash</strong></td><td>Shows your actual return on invested dollars</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Stress-testing a deal</td><td><strong>Both</strong></td><td>Run both; if cap rate &lt; your mortgage rate, CoC will be negative</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Comparing to REIT returns</td><td><strong>Cap Rate</strong></td><td>REITs report NOI-based unlevered returns</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Deciding on leverage amount</td><td><strong>CoC + DSCR</strong></td><td>CoC optimizes equity return; DSCR ensures loan qualification</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

